WEBVTT

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:08.610
For summer vacation...

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:11.110
we should have a training camp, right?

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:12.240
We should!

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:14.240
No way. That sounds like hassle.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:17.120
I-Is this opposition I hear?!

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:20.540
What kind of training does this club even need to do?

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:22.660
Fine-tuning our card game decks?

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:24.790
We don't need a training camp for that.

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:27.460
But we can't beat those elementary school dweebs if we don't!

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.670
We don't have to do that.

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:31.340
We could also carefully breed the best IVs,

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:34.180
then train our EVs and form dueling parties.

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:36.180
We can play those games at home, too.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:39.060
Nuh-uh! I wanna have a training camp!

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:41.810
What did I do to deserve this, Natsuki?!

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:43.060
Say it from the heart...

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:46.310
Say it from the heart, and I'll consider it.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:52.530
Stare...

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:57.070
I want...

00:00:57.820 --> 00:00:59.620
all of us to go on a trip together.

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:35.630
So...

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:38.130
Having decided to hold a training camp,

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:42.680
we are now faced with what could
be called the ultimate decision.

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:44.100
In other words!

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:45.510
Should we go with the mountains...

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:47.270
Or...

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:49.140
the village?

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:53.400
If you're talking about the candy, just take both kinds!

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:57.860
Why don't we seal both types in a jar
and take whichever one survives?

00:02:57.860 --> 00:02:59.530
What kind of witch doctor are you?!

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:00.700
Now, now...

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:03.570
Why don't we compromise and just
take a couple of pastry chefs along?

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:05.910
This girl has no intention of compromising!

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:08.040
I'd love to go to the beach!

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:09.460
I'll have to buy a swimsuit.

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:12.210
And this one's ignoring the conversation
and thinking about destinations!

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:13.040
What?

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:16.090
I thought we were talking about
where to go for our training camp.

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:17.250
Well...

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:20.050
that was the original point, but...

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:27.220
But ultimate decisions do crop up
surprisingly often, don't they?

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:29.060
Dogs or cats?!

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:30.680
That's a duel of cuteness.

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:31.940
Udon or soba?!

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:33.940
Doesn't that depend onwhat you're in the mood for?

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:36.230
Should your starter be a fire type or a water type?

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:37.820
Yeah, no one goes for grass.

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:39.610
Ayanami or Shikinami?!

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:42.110
You mean, choose between the
aloof crush and the psycho crush?

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:44.110
No, I think she means the warships.

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:45.950
Going Home Club or Watamote?

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:48.040
We can't say much about that...

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:51.870
We really do run up against a lot of choices.

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:55.210
As the one carrying on the name of Hagitsuki-ryuu,

00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:57.500
I frequently have to choose whether I live or die.

00:03:57.500 --> 00:03:59.960
Not much of a choice to make there.

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:01.880
But even if I get past that...

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:05.890
I'm still faced with the decision of whether to have

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:07.640
my red bean paste smooth or chunky!

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:09.060
It doesn't even matter!

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:10.430
That's hardly life or death!

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:12.140
Normally, I prefer smooth,

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:14.770
but sometimes, chunky is better in red bean pancakes.

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:18.400
Why do you worry more about that than about living or dying?

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:24.030
But when I think about the ultimate
decision, you know what I think of?

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:26.820
In the fifth game of the Epic RPG series,

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:30.040
do you marry your childhood friend or the rich girl?

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:32.040
That one comes up a lot,

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:34.920
but in practice, isn't the childhood friend the only real choice?

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:37.330
I mean, it's between the childhood friend who idolizes

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:40.840
the protagonist and wishes for his happiness more than her own...

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:42.720
or some rich girl who came out of nowhere!

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:44.930
Who'd pick the rich one?

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:46.300
Someone obsessed with money?

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:49.180
Why is that image on the screen?

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:52.140
There's a little thing in this world called "grown-up stuff."

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:54.940
Yeah, we'd get in trouble if we drew
characters that look too much like them.

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:58.860
Now that you mention it,
I chose the childhood friend, too.

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:01.690
I also chose the childhood friend my first time around.

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:02.860
That's right.

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:05.530
It really doesn't matter if she has money.

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:07.950
That's really irritating coming from her.

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:12.540
The childhood friend and the rich girl
both use different magic too, don't they?

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:14.120
There are probably a lot of people

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:16.620
who chose the rich girl because they wanted her spells.

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:23.460
Sealsplosion!

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:25.920
What are you trying to say?!

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:28.090
There's more to a woman's worth
than what magic she uses!

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:29.550
That's right!

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:31.470
Sakura, you're so cool!

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:33.060
That's our president!

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:35.180
That's a fair argument,

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:38.060
but regular girls can't use attack magic anyway.

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:42.070
But if choosing a bride isn't the ultimate decision,

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:44.400
what else could there be?

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:48.360
There's some famous ones, like um, what was it...

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:52.080
Something about a beautiful woman...
and something about curry flavors.

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:54.410
Yes! I know that one!

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:59.040
Would you rather have curry with a
great personality or a sh*t-flavored hag?

00:06:01.790 --> 00:06:03.090
What kind of choice is that?

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:05.460
Curry with a personality doesn't even make sense!

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:07.800
And a "sh*t-flavored hag" is just sad!

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:09.180
Natsuki, calm down!

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:12.180
It's bad for our image if the heroine
says "sh*t, sh*t" all the time!

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:13.720
Sakura, calm down!

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:16.680
You're only ending up rep**ting "sh*t" yourself!

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:18.560
You don't have to censor "repeating"!

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:21.810
The winds of Ihatovo are crystal clear...

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:25.980
The blue sky is refreshingly cool, even in summer.

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:29.070
Picturesque forests frame the city of Morio,

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:32.200
and just outside the city are glittering waves of grass...

00:06:32.570 --> 00:06:37.200
Botan's beautiful words cleansed
this place of the stink of curry.

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:40.210
Is there some meaning behind those lines?

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:43.750
That was Air Refresh Logos.

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:45.460
It has a skill name?!

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:48.470
Back to life!

00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:53.850
But some "ultimate decisions" have
more than just two choices, right?

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:55.010
For instance:

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:59.100
"If you could only eat one thing
for a year, what would it be?"

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:00.100
Like that.

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:02.730
Of course, there are those who would say

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:05.270
"The daily special!" with a know-it-all smirk.

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:07.150
But that gag expired before even

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:09.150
the daily special did, so that's off-limits.

00:07:09.150 --> 00:07:11.740
Did you have a bad experience with that or something?

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:14.580
Keeping that in mind, I'd go with hot pot.

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:15.620
H*t p*t?

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:18.950
Karin, you don't have to censor "hot pot."

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:21.120
You like stew, Sakura?

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:25.790
In the world of sumo, all foods are called "hot pot."

00:07:25.790 --> 00:07:27.880
Then that's no different from choosing the daily special!

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:29.380
Botan,

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:32.800
if you could only eat one food, what would it be?

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:34.090
Let me think...

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:36.140
I just can't decide.

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:38.640
Smooth or chunky red bean paste...

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:40.560
You're stuck on that decision again?!

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:42.730
I think I might go with flan!

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:45.900
I think I'd get sick of that on the first day.

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:47.270
What about you, Natsuki?

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:51.320
I'd go with...

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:53.950
Omelet rice.

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:58.450
Cut that out!

00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:00.160
Sealet rice!

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:01.620
More importantly!

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:04.920
We need to pick where to go
for our training camp already.

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:06.630
Oh, that's right.

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:09.510
I still want to go to the beach!

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:11.880
I'd prefer the mountains, myself.

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:16.720
It might be nice to reserve the
Palace of Versailles for a private tour.

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:19.600
Everyone! We're going to a training camp!

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:21.390
We aren't going for fun!

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:25.150
Then, where do you think we
should go, Sakura?

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:29.230
Kagawa!

00:08:34.070 --> 00:08:36.780
We're going to go to Kagawa to annihilate udon!

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:38.120
Kagawa?

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:39.450
Annihilate?

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:40.740
Udon?

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:52.800
Going Home Club crosses the ocean!

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:55.800
When we go home, we'll have to cross the ocean again!

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:56.840
Ahem.

00:08:57.090 --> 00:09:00.310
And so, we of the Going Home Club have arrived

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:02.140
at our summer vacation training camp.

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:05.730
So this is the land of udon!

00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:08.900
This looks a lot like Ogikubo to me.

00:09:09.150 --> 00:09:12.730
That's because Ogikubo's famous
throughout the industry for its cuisine.

00:09:12.730 --> 00:09:17.410
For various reasons, the scenery
of Ogikubo has been applied here.

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:20.740
Did the staff only go location hunting locally?

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:24.370
More importantly, let's begin our Udon Annihilation Plan!

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:26.000
Let's start...

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:27.370
with this store!

00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:36.880
So good!

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:39.340
This is the flavor of the real deal!

00:09:42.510 --> 00:09:45.230
There. It's cool enough now, Karin.

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:48.150
Is it good?

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:50.150
Yes, it's yummy.

00:09:50.150 --> 00:09:52.400
You're spoiling her yet again.

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:55.030
I'm afraid...

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:57.650
I can't eat this udon.

00:09:58.610 --> 00:09:59.950
Because it's...

00:10:01.030 --> 00:10:02.410
steaming hot!

00:10:02.410 --> 00:10:03.660
She's sensitive to hot food?

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:05.040
No, no, no!

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:07.790
I can't eat it unless someone blows on it for me!

00:10:07.790 --> 00:10:09.290
You're hopeless.

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:17.630
Cold.

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:19.760
Next, this store!

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:21.220
I know it's late to bring this up,

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:24.560
but I get the feeling this "Udon
Annihilation Plan" is just a culinary tour.

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:33.400
Please try to not splatter your
curry udon broth everywhere.

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:35.610
Okay, okay, don't sweat it.

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:41.820
Speaking of curry udon, I realized I
misremembered that thing I said before.

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:44.410
What I meant to say was curry-flavored sh—

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:56.050
And so I will quietly recount my time in Ihatovo,

00:10:56.550 --> 00:10:59.760
split over a number of short chapters...

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:00.720
There it is!

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:03.010
Botan's Air Refresh Logos!

00:11:03.510 --> 00:11:06.890
No, that skill won't get out curry stains.

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:15.070
The hot water is so nice!

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:17.190
It sure is!

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:18.280
But...

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:20.530
Why are we in a cauldron-shaped bath?

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:22.950
Well, we <i>are</i> in the land of Udon.

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:25.410
We'll boil ourselves in a pot for sleek, smooth skin!

00:11:27.950 --> 00:11:30.460
Hey, our futons are all laid out.

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:32.210
Which means...

00:11:33.750 --> 00:11:35.750
Let the pillow fight begin!

00:11:41.090 --> 00:11:42.010
You're open!

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:47.760
Ow... ow...

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:50.770
At least try to hold back a little...

00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:58.690
Wow, so pretty!

00:12:15.380 --> 00:12:16.460
There, look at that.

00:12:16.460 --> 00:12:18.380
That's the Andromeda constellation.

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:19.840
Hold on a minute.

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:23.220
Isn't Andromeda an autumn constellation?

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:26.010
Why can we see it in summer?

00:12:26.010 --> 00:12:29.140
Oh, that's because we're in the land of Udon.

00:12:29.140 --> 00:12:32.520
The change in latitude means we see
different stars than in Honshu.

00:12:32.770 --> 00:12:35.850
But how is that Andromeda?

00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:37.270
Well, because of this...

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:41.990
What? Was there always so much
adult content in the night sky?

00:12:41.990 --> 00:12:44.740
In ancient times, the night sky was
the only entertainment people had.

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:48.370
It was a dark era where the sky shone full of stars.

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:53.210
The people back then would look up at
the night sky and think things like:

00:12:53.210 --> 00:12:55.460
"Do those stars look like boobs to you?"

00:12:55.460 --> 00:12:58.130
"Sure do! I bet they're F-cups!"

00:12:58.130 --> 00:13:00.300
You're taking your imagination too far!

00:13:00.300 --> 00:13:05.260
Which must mean that those
two stars were used like this...

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:06.180
Despicable!

00:13:06.180 --> 00:13:07.930
Ancient people were despicable!

00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:09.890
How does this look?

00:13:10.180 --> 00:13:14.060
According to the legend, there was a
whale that tried to eat Andromeda,

00:13:14.060 --> 00:13:16.600
and he has a constellation, too.

00:13:17.690 --> 00:13:19.020
Something like this?

00:13:19.020 --> 00:13:21.190
Oh, you've got the idea.

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:23.150
But the correct answer is this!

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:23.690
Look!

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:24.690
Boom!

00:13:24.690 --> 00:13:26.400
How is that a whale?

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:28.240
It looks like a naked mole rat.

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:30.830
Strictly speaking, it's actually a sea monster, but...

00:13:30.830 --> 00:13:33.290
He's a serious nuisance to real whales.

00:13:33.290 --> 00:13:36.670
In addition, the tyranny in the stars never ends!

00:13:36.670 --> 00:13:38.920
Here! What constellation do you think this is?

00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:42.420
Three stars... It's very simplistic.

00:13:42.670 --> 00:13:44.420
A caterpillar constellation?

00:13:44.710 --> 00:13:46.170
It's Vulpecula, a little fox!

00:13:46.420 --> 00:13:48.340
Gon, is that you?

00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:51.050
So human imagination has come this far?

00:13:51.050 --> 00:13:53.430
It's as endless as the universe, it seems.

00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:55.100
Here's another three-star constellation!

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:56.430
What is it?

00:13:56.430 --> 00:13:58.850
The last one was a fox, so...

00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:00.810
This must be something amazing too, right?

00:14:00.810 --> 00:14:02.770
Like an anomalocaris constellation or something.

00:14:02.770 --> 00:14:04.230
It's Triangulum, the triangle!

00:14:04.230 --> 00:14:06.530
Why is this one so normal?!

00:14:06.530 --> 00:14:09.490
There's an unconvincing outrageousness to it all!

00:14:09.490 --> 00:14:12.240
This is the tyranny of imagination!

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:14.490
If that kind of thing is allowed, then...

00:14:14.490 --> 00:14:16.660
I want us to be like this from now on!

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:18.160
A-Are you a genius?

00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:20.080
Now we should get the episode out on time.

00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:21.590
No, that's asking too much.

00:14:21.590 --> 00:14:23.840
From now on, we can just sketch out the major points,

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:26.720
and leave the rest to the viewers' imagination.

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:29.380
Sakura, why are you taking off your clothes?

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:32.260
Sakura, you can't eat that!

00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:34.600
Stop that! Don't treat your body so carelessly!

00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:36.730
What is even going on?!

00:14:37.140 --> 00:14:41.440
And so, the Going Home Club's training
camp continued deep into the night.

00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:47.820
That was the training we did before going home!

00:14:50.360 --> 00:14:52.990
These are our club activities after getting home!

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:07.760
So hot...

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:16.810
So cool!

00:15:16.810 --> 00:15:19.350
The heat's no excuse for the staff to slack off!

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:25.480
There!

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:28.860
I can't believe you're eating
ice cream right after waking up.

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:31.360
And it's toothpaste flavor?

00:15:31.360 --> 00:15:34.320
Are you dissing my mint chocolate chip?

00:15:34.490 --> 00:15:36.830
You actually want to eat some, don't ya?

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:38.410
N-No, thanks.

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:40.210
Here, open up!

00:15:40.210 --> 00:15:42.000
I just said I didn't want it!

00:15:42.170 --> 00:15:43.420
Just kidding!

00:15:43.670 --> 00:15:45.170
None for you!

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:47.250
I'm not even slightly jealous!

00:15:55.100 --> 00:15:56.970
Oh, it's Sakura.

00:15:57.220 --> 00:15:58.140
Hello?

00:15:58.140 --> 00:16:00.850
Hello! Is this Natsuki of the Dead?

00:16:00.850 --> 00:16:02.190
Who're you callin' a zombie?!

00:16:04.310 --> 00:16:06.270
Huh? You're all going to the pool?

00:16:06.770 --> 00:16:08.650
Yeah, I'll go!

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:12.150
Hooray!

00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:16.780
It was already reserved for my family today.

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:19.620
So don't worry and just enjoy yourself.

00:16:30.170 --> 00:16:31.210
Take that!

00:16:42.100 --> 00:16:44.810
I wonder if they'll turn all of
this into fanservice shots...

00:16:46.600 --> 00:16:48.730
Huh? Where's Botan?

00:16:48.730 --> 00:16:50.820
She said she was going to
train in the shower first.

00:16:56.990 --> 00:16:59.410
Even if you think you've acquired freedom...

00:16:59.410 --> 00:17:03.620
you may just be trapped in another
cage that goes by the name of freedom.

00:17:03.620 --> 00:17:05.250
Where did that come from?

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:12.920
I was just thinking... in competitive
swimming, there's a "freestyle,"

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:16.630
but people only actually choose the crawl.

00:17:17.510 --> 00:17:18.930
That's true.

00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:21.930
If everyone does the crawl,
you shouldn't call it freestyle.

00:17:21.930 --> 00:17:24.560
You should call it Crawl Second Chance.

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:27.400
Though, if someone did the doggy paddle
because they felt they couldn't win,

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:29.650
it'd be more memorable than
the swimmers who set records.

00:17:29.650 --> 00:17:31.900
You still have to do your best.

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:34.030
If this were badminton, you'd get disqualified.

00:17:34.030 --> 00:17:36.450
Yeah, that was pretty memorable.

00:17:36.450 --> 00:17:38.700
Though, I forget the names of the players.

00:17:38.700 --> 00:17:40.990
I wonder if you could use a kick board...

00:17:40.990 --> 00:17:42.830
That really <i>would</i> be freestyle!

00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:46.040
But people who still need those wouldn't
participate, so I don't know!

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:48.420
I wonder if you could use a cruiser.

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:50.380
That's obviously out!

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:52.380
You wouldn't be swimming then.

00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:54.170
Then, that's the real question.

00:17:54.170 --> 00:17:57.760
What do the rules define as "swimming"?

00:17:57.760 --> 00:17:58.640
Huh?

00:17:58.640 --> 00:18:01.180
For instance, if you ran over the surface of the water,

00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:04.390
would that be considered
acceptable "freestyle swimming"?

00:18:05.180 --> 00:18:07.640
I imagine Botan could do that.

00:18:07.890 --> 00:18:10.690
No way. Not even Botan could...

00:18:10.690 --> 00:18:13.230
Hey, everyone!

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:16.900
Sorry for making you wait!

00:18:33.380 --> 00:18:35.000
When I think about it,

00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:37.720
the really frustrating thing might
not be "freedom in name only,"

00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:39.880
but half-baked freedom.

00:18:39.880 --> 00:18:42.300
Half-baked freedom?

00:18:42.300 --> 00:18:45.430
Yes. For instance, summer vacation research projects.

00:18:45.720 --> 00:18:47.100
They say you can pick anything,

00:18:47.100 --> 00:18:48.560
but there's still pressure

00:18:48.560 --> 00:18:50.940
to not pick something too random.

00:18:50.940 --> 00:18:52.060
You're right.

00:18:52.060 --> 00:18:54.690
There's such a thing as "freedom with restrictions."

00:18:55.780 --> 00:18:58.240
I can't count how many times
I've thought about collecting

00:18:58.240 --> 00:19:00.570
pushy teachers and turning <i>them</i> in as samples.

00:19:00.570 --> 00:19:02.530
She comes up with scary ideas.

00:19:02.530 --> 00:19:05.950
Speaking of which, Natsuki, what
kind of research projects have you done?

00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:09.210
I made a disappointing shishi-odoshi.

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:10.920
What? A disappointing one?

00:19:11.210 --> 00:19:14.170
It doesn't bonk on the ground when it fills up.

00:19:14.170 --> 00:19:16.130
That's a novel kind of shishi-odoshi.

00:19:16.550 --> 00:19:20.680
And I made a piggy bank that lets you
save 250 yen of a 500 yen coin.

00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:23.260
That doesn't sound like a very useful bank.

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:25.890
Well, I figured it didn't matter.

00:19:25.890 --> 00:19:30.690
Natsuki, you seem very anti-establishment
when it comes to your summer homework.

00:19:30.690 --> 00:19:33.560
I watched the 7 AM news every day and counted

00:19:33.560 --> 00:19:36.650
the number of times the newscaster
fumbled over her words.

00:19:36.650 --> 00:19:38.320
That's an unpleasant outlook.

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:39.860
As a result,

00:19:39.860 --> 00:19:41.780
I learned that even pros make a lot of mistakes,

00:19:41.780 --> 00:19:45.070
and that there are a lot of things in
this world that will never be free.

00:19:45.070 --> 00:19:47.330
That sounds like very worthwhile research.

00:19:47.330 --> 00:19:48.370
Yes.

00:19:48.370 --> 00:19:53.420
So it's not really possible for
us to acquire true freedom.

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:55.460
That's true.

00:19:55.460 --> 00:20:00.220
Grown-up stuff and company intentions
will always put restrictions on us.

00:20:01.050 --> 00:20:01.970
Yeah.

00:20:02.760 --> 00:20:06.510
After all, when we just wanted to
talk about Epic RPG a little bit...

00:20:07.390 --> 00:20:09.220
it ended up like this.

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:38.880
Freedom is merely an illusion.

00:20:40.460 --> 00:20:42.920
It doesn't exist anywhere in this world.

00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:55.060
You know...

00:20:59.940 --> 00:21:03.440
There's nowhere left to go with this
subject, so let's end the episode here!

00:21:03.440 --> 00:21:05.360
That's <i>too</i> free!

00:22:46.210 --> 00:22:50.760
The Rhinogradentia, or Snouter, turns upside down
and walks on its nose, as the name suggests.

00:22:50.760 --> 00:22:53.510
The world really is full of mysterious things!

00:22:57.020 --> 00:22:59.270
And a couple of others!
